From 049a56c209f1e4c39bf4d72c5847f9ff453aebbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:44:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] feat(lanes): worker ceilings, nullable valves and
 dependency blockers

Persist max_workers alongside lane configuration, filter ready/review candidates
and recheck the observed running count at the local claim CAS. Zero stops new
claims; null leaves existing behavior unchanged. Existing fleet census is used;
this is not an atomic cross-gateway reservation (documented explicitly).

Distinguish omitted daily limits from explicit null; expose repeatable --unset
and --max-workers in lanes set. Report all open parent IDs and their PRs on dep
waits, preserving first blocker shorthand and avoiding own-card PR inference.

Proof: initial regression RED 5 failures; GREEN 16 consumer/docs files, 289 tests
passed, zero failed. Claim-ceiling removal mutant killed by six regressions.
Full scripts/check --base origin/main passed. Plugin compatibility lives in the
companion hermes-mods change; no production configuration changed.
